    <decisions>
        <description>We will assign the correct email subject, body, and cc recipient based on the Case&apos;s Subject</description>
        <name>What_is_the_Case_Subject</name>
        <label>What is the Case Subject?</label>
        <locationX>0</locationX>
        <locationY>0</locationY>
        <defaultConnectorLabel>Other</defaultConnectorLabel>
        <rules>
            <name>Increase_Cap</name>
            <conditionLogic>and</conditionLogic>
            <conditions>
                <leftValueReference>$Record.Subject</leftValueReference>
                <operator>EqualTo</operator>
                <rightValue>
                    <stringValue>Increase Cap - High Fill Rate Area</stringValue>
                </rightValue>
            </conditions>
            <connector>
                <targetReference>Assign_Email_Body_Subject_Increase_Cap</targetReference>
            </connector>
            <label>Increase Cap</label>
        </rules>
        <rules>
            <name>Billing_Errors</name>
            <conditionLogic>and</conditionLogic>
            <conditions>
                <leftValueReference>$Record.Subject</leftValueReference>
                <operator>EqualTo</operator>
                <rightValue>
                    <stringValue>Account Health - Account Has Billing Error(s)</stringValue>
                </rightValue>
            </conditions>
            <connector>
                <targetReference>Assign_Email_Body_Subject_Billing_Errors</targetReference>
            </connector>
            <label>Billing Errors</label>
        </rules>
    </decisions>
    <description>When an Account Management case is created with the Topic &quot;Evergreen Automation&quot;, check the Subject and Account Type, then send the appropriate email.

Subject is &quot;Increase Cap - High Fill Rate Area&quot; or &quot;Account Health - Account Has Billing Error(s)&quot; - send appropriate email. Other subject, do nothing.

S3P-1134 - Created.
S3P-1291 - Moved actions to a scheduled path to prevent locked row error from mass simple loader update.
S3P-1345 - Updated scheduled path to wait an hour. Simplified logic by using formulas to prepare for addition of more emails in future.
S3P-1346 - Added Billing Error email. Updated start criteria to exclude Contacts without an email or that have opted out of email.
Hot Fix - Emails with &quot;other&quot; subject should not be sending an email, flow should end.</description>
    <environments>Default</environments>
    <formulas>
        <name>Formula_ActiveAccountWithSupportRep</name>
        <dataType>Boolean</dataType>
        <expression>IF(
    AND(
             OR(
                     ISPICKVAL({!$Record.Account.Type}, &quot;Core&quot;),
                     ISPICKVAL({!$Record.Account.Type}, &quot;Accelerated-AGP&quot;),
                     ISPICKVAL({!$Record.Account.Type}, &quot;Accelerated-AGP Premier&quot;)
              ),
             NOT(ISBLANK({!$Record.Account.Support_Rep__c})),
             {!$Record.Account.Support_Rep__r.IsActive}
     ),
TRUE, FALSE)</expression>
    </formulas>
    <formulas>
        <description>If the Account has a support rep, display their calendar link to be added at the bottom of the email body. Otherwise display nothing.</description>
        <name>Formula_EmailBody_CalendarLink</name>
        <dataType>String</dataType>
        <expression>IF(
    {!Formula_ActiveAccountWithSupportRep},
    &quot;&lt;a href=&apos;&quot; + {!$Record.Account.Support_Rep__r.Salesforce_Meeting_Link__c} + &quot;&apos; target=&apos;_blank&apos;&gt;Book time with me&lt;/a&gt;&quot;,
    null
)</expression>
    </formulas>
    <formulas>
        <description>If the Account has an active support rep (and is currently Core, AGP, or Premier), the email signature should be the Support Rep, otherwise it should be &quot;The EverQuote Customer Support Team&quot;</description>
        <name>Formula_EmailBody_Signer</name>
        <dataType>String</dataType>
        <expression>IF({!Formula_ActiveAccountWithSupportRep}, {!$Record.Account.Support_Rep__r.FirstName} &amp; &quot; &quot; &amp;{!$Record.Account.Support_Rep__r.LastName},
&quot;The EverQuote Customer Support Team&quot;
)</expression>
    </formulas>
    <formulas>
        <description>Returns either the Account Support Rep or blank depending on the Account Type</description>
        <name>Formula_EmailCC</name>
        <dataType>String</dataType>
        <expression>IF(
    {!Formula_ActiveAccountWithSupportRep},
     {!$Record.Account.Support_Rep__r.Email}, /*CC account support rep if Account Type is Core or AGP */
      &quot;&quot; /* Leave CC blank because Starter accounts shouldn&apos;t CC anyone */
)</expression>
    </formulas>
    <interviewLabel>Case_AccountManagement_Evergreen_Created_SendEmail {!$Flow.CurrentDateTime}</interviewLabel>
    <label>Case_AccountManagement_Evergreen_Created_SendEmail</label>
    <processMetadataValues>
        <name>BuilderType</name>
        <value>
            <stringValue>LightningFlowBuilder</stringValue>
        </value>
    </processMetadataValues>
    <processMetadataValues>
        <name>CanvasMode</name>
        <value>
            <stringValue>AUTO_LAYOUT_CANVAS</stringValue>
        </value>
    </processMetadataValues>
    <processMetadataValues>
        <name>OriginBuilderType</name>
        <value>
            <stringValue>LightningFlowBuilder</stringValue>
        </value>
    </processMetadataValues>
    <processType>AutoLaunchedFlow</processType>
    <start>
        <locationX>0</locationX>
        <locationY>0</locationY>
        <filterFormula>AND(
         {!$Record.RecordType.DeveloperName} = &quot;Account_Management&quot;,
         ISPICKVAL({!$Record.Topic__c}, &quot;Evergreen&quot;),
         NOT(ISBLANK({!$Record.ContactId})),
         NOT(ISBLANK({!$Record.Contact.Email})),
         ISBLANK({!$Record.Contact.EmailBouncedReason}),
         NOT({!$Record.Contact.HasOptedOutOfEmail}),
         {!$Record.Do_Not_Send_Automated_Email__c} = FALSE
)</filterFormula>
        <object>Case</object>
        <recordTriggerType>Create</recordTriggerType>
        <scheduledPaths>
            <name>X1_Hour_After_Creation</name>
            <connector>
                <targetReference>What_is_the_Case_Subject</targetReference>
            </connector>
            <label>1 Hour After Creation</label>
            <offsetNumber>1</offsetNumber>
            <offsetUnit>Hours</offsetUnit>
            <timeSource>RecordTriggerEvent</timeSource>
        </scheduledPaths>
        <triggerType>RecordAfterSave</triggerType>
    </start>
    <status>Active</status>
